# Optional overrides — nextiva-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via two request headers, matching MSPbots'
# own stored credential fields for this integration (Nextiva's contact
# center platform is built on Thrio):
#   X-Nextiva-Username — the Thrio account username (Admin-configured)
#   X-Nextiva-Password — the corresponding password
#
# This server performs a fresh 2-step call on every single tool call:
#   1. GET https://login.thrio.com/provider/token-with-authorities with
#      HTTP Basic Auth (username:password) -> {"location": "https://<tenant
#      cluster>.thrio.io", "token": "..."} — the "location" is the actual
#      per-tenant API host, resolved dynamically (never hardcoded), and the
#      token is used as-is (no "Bearer " prefix) in an "Authorization" header.
#   2. The real data call to "{location}/data/api/types/..." or
#      "{location}/analytics/api/v1/types/..." with that Authorization header.
# Nothing is cached or persisted across MCP calls.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
